$$v_i(t) = 1 \quad \text{for all } i = 1, \dots, 6$$
$$x_i(t) \equiv 1 \pmod 2 \quad \text{for all } i = 1, \dots, 6$$

This implies that for each switch $i$, the number of times it was flipped, $x_i(t)$, must be an odd integer.
Let $x_i(t) = 2a_i + 1$ for some non-negative integer $a_i$.

